{"name":"Armageddon Dunes","hex":"#926a25","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"armageddon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Armageddon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/armageddon"},{"term":"dunes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of dune"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dunes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Armageddon","blocks":[{"text":"Armageddon is the prophesied gathering of armies for a battle during the end times, according to the Book of Revelation in the New Testament of the Christian Bible. Armageddon is variously interpreted as either a literal or a symbolic location, although the term has since become more often used in a generic sense to refer to any end-of-the-world scenario. In Islamic theology, Armageddon is also mentioned in Hadith as the Greatest War or Al-Malhama Al-Kubra."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armageddon","wikidata":"Q193151"},{"title":"Dune","blocks":[{"text":"A dune is a landform composed of wind- or water-driven sand. It typically takes the form of a mound, ridge, or hill. An area with dunes is called a dune system or a dune complex. A large dune complex is called a dune field, while broad, flat regions covered with wind-swept sand or dunes, with little or no vegetation, are called ergs or sand seas. Dunes occur in different shapes and sizes, but most kinds of dunes are longer on the stoss (upflow) side, where the sand is pushed up the dune, and have a shorter slip face in the lee side. The valley or trough between dunes is called a dune slack."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg/330px-Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune","wikidata":"Q25391"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Johannes_op_Patmos_Saint_John_on_Patmos_Berlin%2C_Staatlichen_Museen_zu_Berlin%2C_Gemaldegalerie_HR.jpg/500px-Johannes_op_Patmos_Saint_John_on_Patmos_Berlin%2C_Staatlichen_Museen_zu_Berlin%2C_Gemaldegalerie_HR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Johannes_op_Patmos_Saint_John_on_Patmos_Berlin%2C_Staatlichen_Museen_zu_Berlin%2C_Gemaldegalerie_HR.jpg/1280px-Johannes_op_Patmos_Saint_John_on_Patmos_Berlin%2C_Staatlichen_Museen_zu_Berlin%2C_Gemaldegalerie_HR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Johannes_op_Patmos_Saint_John_on_Patmos_Berlin%2C_Staatlichen_Museen_zu_Berlin%2C_Gemaldegalerie_HR.jpg/500px-Johannes_op_Patmos_Saint_John_on_Patmos_Berlin%2C_Staatlichen_Museen_zu_Berlin%2C_Gemaldegalerie_HR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Saint John the Evangelist on Patmos. Painting by Hieronymus Bosch (1505).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohannes_op_Patmos_Saint_John_on_Patmos_Berlin%2C_Staatlichen_Museen_zu_Berlin%2C_Gemaldegalerie_HR.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/%D7%AA%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%93%D7%95.JPG/500px-%D7%AA%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%93%D7%95.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/%D7%AA%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%93%D7%95.JPG/1280px-%D7%AA%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%93%D7%95.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/%D7%AA%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%93%D7%95.JPG/500px-%D7%AA%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%93%D7%95.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tel Megiddo with archaeological remains from the Bronze and Iron Ages","link":"https://en.wikipedia.or